1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,120
Functional capacity is

2
00:00:01,140 --> 00:00:02,400
one of the strongest predictors

3
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:03,680
of how well you’ll age.

4
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,720
Starting in our 30s,

5
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:06,080
we gradually lose muscle mass,

6
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,200
and the loss speeds up

7
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:08,160
as we get older.

8
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:09,200
Less muscle mass means

9
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:10,000
less stability,

10
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:10,960
slower reactions,

11
00:00:10,980 --> 00:00:12,560
and a higher risk of falls.

12
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:13,280
The good news is that

13
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:14,480
this is very trainable

14
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:15,280
at any age,

15
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:15,920
but you have to

16
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:16,880
measure it first.

17
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:17,520
So when we look at

18
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:18,640
functional capacity,

19
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:19,840
we ask three things.

20
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:21,680
One, can you move with control?

21
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:22,880
Two, can you maintain

22
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:23,920
your range of motion?

23
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:25,280
Three, are you strong enough

24
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:26,640
for every stage of life?

25
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,000
Functional capacity isn’t

26
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:29,440
just about how you move today.

27
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:30,400
It’s about protecting

28
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:31,520
what you’ll be able to do

29
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:34,000
10, 20, 30 years from now.

30
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:35,200
At Vexon Med,

31
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:36,240
we measure it so we can

32
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:37,520
build a plan around it.

33
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:38,640
Click the link in our bio

34
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:40,340
to book your assessment.
